1
00:00:03,721 --> 00:00:05,207
Full of Surprises

2
00:00:05,207 --> 00:00:06,852
Don't tell me.

3
00:00:06,852 --> 00:00:09,184
Please don't tell me.

4
00:00:09,184 --> 00:00:09,934
I recognize you ...

5
00:00:09,934 --> 00:00:15,690
Oh, don't be silly, Arnie.

6
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:18,535
Of course you recognize him.

7
00:00:18,535 --> 00:01:26,361
Except for the beard, he hasn't changed in fifty years.

8
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:27,861
It's Malcolm Stewart!

9
00:01:27,861 --> 00:01:31,499
I know it's Malcolm Stewart.

10
00:01:31,499 --> 00:01:39,416
You haven't changed much in fifty years.

11
00:01:39,416 --> 00:01:41,251
Peggy--Peggy Pendleton!

12
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:44,229
You're Peggy Pendleton!

13
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:47,207
Who am I, you old rascal?

14
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:49,207
You don't recognize me, do you?

15
00:01:49,207 --> 00:01:50,935
I know who you are.

16
00:01:50,935 --> 00:01:51,852
You're Arnold Franklin!

17
00:01:51,852 --> 00:01:54,163
I know who you are!

18
00:01:54,163 --> 00:01:56,140
You look wonderful, Malcolm!

19
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,444
Sit down. Sit down.

20
00:01:58,444 --> 00:02:06,074
Pete isn't home.

21
00:02:06,074 --> 00:02:06,574
Really?

22
00:02:06,574 --> 00:02:09,552
No. He left a note on the door

23
00:02:09,552 --> 00:02:13,807
saying he was going to the railroad station

24
00:02:13,807 --> 00:02:14,675
to pick up a surprise.

25
00:02:14,675 --> 00:02:15,675
He's so funny.

26
00:02:15,675 --> 00:02:19,095
Always full of surprises,

27
00:02:19,095 --> 00:02:19,964
even fifty years later.

28
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:24,942
The two of you look unbelievable!

29
00:02:24,942 --> 00:02:25,920
How's your family?

30
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:26,920
Oh, I was sorry

31
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,275
to hear about your wife having passed away.

32
00:02:29,275 --> 00:02:31,876
Yes. About four years ago.

33
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:34,854
And you're living with your children now? In New York?

34
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:36,134
Pete wrote us and told us.

35
00:02:36,134 --> 00:02:37,134
Yup.

36
00:02:37,134 --> 00:02:40,810
Retired and moved to New York

37
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:43,788
to live with my son and his family.

38
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:44,541
By the way,

39
00:02:44,541 --> 00:02:48,433
what do you think this big surprise is?

40
00:02:48,433 --> 00:02:56,200
It could be most anything, knowing Pete.

41
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:59,878
Hey, that must be Pete!

42
00:02:59,878 --> 00:03:07,612
Now we'll find out about the surprise.

43
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:13,567
So good to see you all!

44
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:19,295
Oh, Pete, Pete!

45
00:03:19,295 --> 00:03:23,221
Oh, it's so good to see you!

46
00:03:23,221 --> 00:03:24,661
Remember Lillian?

47
00:03:24,661 --> 00:03:28,941
I remember all of you.

48
00:03:28,941 --> 00:03:30,395
You haven't changed a bit.

49
00:03:30,395 --> 00:03:31,686
Lillian! Oh, my gosh! Lillian

50
00:03:31,686 --> 00:03:32,690
Lillian Winters. Lillian Winters

51
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:37,391
We were together in the Thursday night drama society.

52
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:42,512
Remember me, Malcolm?

53
00:03:42,512 --> 00:03:46,325
Oh, beautiful as ever, Lillian.

54
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:47,182
How's Donald? Donald

55
00:03:47,182 --> 00:03:48,039
That's OK, Malcolm.

56
00:03:48,039 --> 00:03:55,259
Donald passed away a couple of years ago.

57
00:03:55,259 --> 00:04:05,193
Sorry to hear that, Lillian.

58
00:04:05,193 --> 00:04:07,171
Oh, I'm so sorry.

59
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:16,105
I would not have missed this get-together for the world!

60
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:20,178
And your little surprise, Pete?

61
00:04:20,178 --> 00:04:22,483
You really surprised me

62
00:04:22,483 --> 00:04:26,467
by having us all come together.

63
00:04:26,467 --> 00:04:30,994
You don't know what the surprise is yet?

64
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:31,994
Come on!

65
00:04:31,994 --> 00:04:38,546
We'll tell you the big surprise.

66
00:04:38,546 --> 00:04:45,306
I've invited you here for the weekend to help celebrate.

67
00:04:45,306 --> 00:04:45,884
Celebrate?

68
00:04:45,884 --> 00:04:47,384
Our fiftieth reunion?

69
00:04:47,384 --> 00:04:47,884
No.

70
00:04:47,884 --> 00:04:54,207
No. Pete wants to tell you ...

71
00:04:54,207 --> 00:04:57,796
Now, let me have the honor, Lillian.

72
00:04:57,796 --> 00:05:00,774
For goodness' sake, Pete, tell us!

73
00:05:00,774 --> 00:05:04,038
I can't wait much longer.

74
00:05:04,038 --> 00:05:06,326
Well, I am pouring this iced tea

75
00:05:06,326 --> 00:05:09,640
so that we can toast Lillian--and me.

76
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:26,741
You don't mean to tell me that you and ...

77
00:05:26,741 --> 00:05:28,243
Yes, I do.

78
00:05:28,243 --> 00:05:35,662
I have loved Lillian all these years,

79
00:05:35,662 --> 00:05:46,776
so I asked her to be Mrs. Pete Waters.

80
00:05:46,776 --> 00:05:49,421
And I said yes.

81
00:05:49,421 --> 00:05:54,377
I knew it! I knew it!

82
00:05:54,377 --> 00:05:54,806
Congratulations!

83
00:05:54,806 --> 00:05:55,663
Oh, Lillian,

84
00:05:55,663 --> 00:05:57,998
I am so happy for you both.

85
00:05:57,998 --> 00:05:58,426
It's wonderful!

86
00:05:58,426 --> 00:05:59,284
It's wonderful for me.

87
00:05:59,284 --> 00:06:01,333
Lillian will make me a happy man--finally.

88
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:04,311
You are full of surprises, Pete.

89
00:06:04,311 --> 00:06:06,860
We are going to

90
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:13,745
spend the entire weekend having a good time together here

91
00:06:13,745 --> 00:06:16,080
on the farm.

92
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:21,179
We are going to celebrate all weekend.

93
00:06:21,179 --> 00:06:25,300
When is the wedding?

94
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:27,135
That's another surprise.

95
00:06:27,135 --> 00:06:56,207
Lillian and I were married two weeks ago in Detroit.

96
00:06:56,207 --> 00:07:01,892
She's come here to stay.

97
00:07:01,892 --> 00:07:04,870
Wait till I tell my family about this!

98
00:07:04,870 --> 00:07:07,870
Why, that's wonderful!
